Falsifies `system_tests::user::supervision_tests::a_child_can_neither_learn_nor_forge_its_label`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is `START` reading the supervision capability out of the reserved fault slot and
leaving it there. The child then holds a capability carrying its own label (and a `READ` view of
its supervisor's endpoint), which is the "learn" half of this test's claim.

Expected to fail: `assert!(table[FAULT_EP_SLOT as usize].is_none(), "the fault slot still holds a
capability after START: the child can read its supervision capability")`. Replayed red on aarch64
on 2026-10-05 (UTC) at that assertion. Not replayed on riscv64 or x86_64 here; CI's re-falsify
job covers them.

**What this record does not cover: the "forge" half.** Its defect would be the kernel writing a
sender's badge into the label register on an ordinary delivery, which is code the kernel does not
have and a patch would have to add to `ipc_receive`'s hot path. That half is a check that the label
register stays `0` for a `SEND` through a capability badged with the very label, and is unfalsified
by patch.

diff --git a/kernel/src/sched.rs b/kernel/src/sched.rs
--- a/kernel/src/sched.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/sched.rs
@@ -5659,7 +5659,6 @@
     {
         t.fault_ep = Some(ep);
         t.fault_label = label;
-        let _ = table.delete(abi::fault::FAULT_EP_SLOT);
     }
     drop(table);
 
